              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a distance, then the Persian for to move away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: نبش",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نبش (nabsh) — \"a (street) corner\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نانوایی در نبش خیابان است. Nânvâyi dar nabsh-e khiyâbân ast. The bakery is on the corner of the street."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Used in addresses: nabsh-e kuche-ye dovvom — on the corner of the second lane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of nabsh is not settled, and EtymDB does not list it. It is the corner where a lane meets a street, and it appears in many Iranian addresses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
