              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پلاک (pelâk) — \"a house number; a number plate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خانه ما پلاک دوازده است. Khâne-ye mâ pelâk-e davâzdah ast. Our house is number twelve."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pelâk-e mâshin — a car's number plate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pelâk was borrowed from French plaque 'a plate, a sheet of metal' (EtymDB): the small metal plate with a house number on it."
            }
          ]
        },
