              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فرعی (far'i) — \"side, minor (of a road); secondary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "از خیابان اصلی وارد یک خیابان فرعی شدیم. Az khiyâbân-e asli vâred-e yek khiyâbân-e far'i shodim. From the main road we turned into a side street."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opposite of asli."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "far'i was borrowed from Arabic and is usually traced to Arabic farʿī 'of a branch', from farʿ 'branch'. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
